# xv6-riscv Security Extension
## Medical Device Security Simulation

**Student:** Hazem Serry  
**Email:** hazemsery15@gmail.com  
**GitHub:** https://github.com/Hazemserry90/xv6-riscv-security

---

## Project Overview

This project extends the **xv6-riscv** teaching operating system with three
kernel-level security layers designed to simulate a medical device security
environment. The implementation adds user authentication, file access control,
and a syscall audit log to the base xv6 kernel.

---

## Security Layers Implemented

### Phase 1 — User Authentication (8 marks)
- Login system with hashed passwords (djb2 algorithm)
- `/etc/passwd` file with pre-populated users
- Four new syscalls: `login`, `useradd`, `userdel`, `passwd`, `whoami`
- Shell access blocked without valid credentials
- Passwords never stored in plaintext

### Phase 2 — File Access Control (8 marks)
- Unix-style permission bits (owner/group/other) on every inode
- `uid` and `gid` fields added to `struct dinode` and `struct inode`
- Two new syscalls: `chmod`, `chown`
- Kernel enforcement in `fileread()`, `filewrite()`, `sys_open()`
- Admin (uid=0) bypasses all permission checks

### Phase 3 — Syscall Audit Log (4 marks)
- Persistent kernel ring buffer (512 entries)
- Every syscall logged with PID, UID, trap name, tick
- Human-readable trap names printed to console
- `audit_read` syscall — admin only (returns EPERM for non-admin)
- End-to-end demo capturing failed logins and permission denials

### Bonus — Compliance Test Suite (5 marks)
- 17 automated test cases across all three phases
- Single command: `comptest`
- Prints `[PASS]` / `[FAIL]` for each test
- Full compliance summary at the end
- Exits with code 0 if all tests pass

---

## Pre-populated Users

| Username | UID | GID | Password   |
|----------|-----|-----|------------|
| admin    | 0   | 0   | admin123   |
| patient  | 1   | 1   | patient123 |
| doctor   | 2   | 2   | doctor123  |

---

## Protected Files

| File                  | Owner | Mode | Description          |
|-----------------------|-------|------|----------------------|
| /patient/records      | uid=1 | 0444 | Patient read-only    |
| /dosage/insulin.log   | uid=2 | 0644 | Doctor write access  |
| /device/config        | uid=0 | 0600 | Admin only           |
| /audit/syscall.log    | uid=0 | 0600 | Admin only           |
| /etc/passwd           | uid=0 | 0644 | User credentials     |

---

## New Syscalls Added

| Syscall      | Number | Description                        |
|--------------|--------|------------------------------------|
| useradd      | 22     | Add new user (admin only)          |
| userdel      | 23     | Delete user (admin only)           |
| passwd       | 24     | Change password                    |
| whoami       | 25     | Print current uid/username         |
| login        | 26     | Authenticate user                  |
| chmod        | 27     | Change file permissions            |
| chown        | 28     | Change file ownership (admin only) |
| audit_read   | 29     | Read audit log (admin only)        |

---

## New Files Created

### Kernel Files
| File                  | Purpose                              |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------|
| kernel/sysauth.c      | Phase 1 authentication syscalls      |
| kernel/audit.c        | Phase 3 ring buffer + audit_read     |

### Modified Kernel Files
| File                  | Changes                              |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------|
| kernel/proc.h         | Added uid, gid to struct proc        |
| kernel/proc.c         | Initialize uid/gid in allocproc()   |
| kernel/fs.h           | Added uid, gid, mode to struct dinode|
| kernel/file.h         | Added uid, gid, mode to struct inode |
| kernel/fs.c           | Copy uid/gid/mode in ilock/iupdate  |
| kernel/file.c         | Permission checks in read/write      |
| kernel/sysfile.c      | chmod/chown + permission in open     |
| kernel/trap.c         | Audit logging + pretty printing      |
| kernel/main.c         | Added audit_init()                   |
| kernel/syscall.h      | New syscall numbers                  |
| kernel/syscall.c      | New syscall table entries            |
| kernel/defs.h         | New function declarations            |
| mkfs/mkfs.c           | Security filesystem structure        |

### User Programs
| File                  | Purpose                              |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------|
| user/login.c          | Login prompt program                 |
| user/whoami.c         | whoami command                       |
| user/useradd.c        | useradd command                      |
| user/userdel.c        | userdel command                      |
| user/passwd.c         | passwd command                       |
| user/chmod.c          | chmod command                        |
| user/chown.c          | chown command                        |
| user/permtest.c       | Permission test program              |
| user/auditdemo.c      | Audit log demo program               |
| user/comptest.c       | Automated compliance test suite      |

---

## How to Build and Run

### Requirements
- RISC-V GCC toolchain (riscv64-linux-gnu-gcc)
- QEMU >= 7.2 (qemu-system-riscv64)
